Hmm, but strictly speaking, "No — I am not authorized to work in the country where this role is based" is a positive claim of non-authorization, and it could be false (the candidate might be a US citizen and the posting might be US). Hmm. But the doctrine in AGENTS.md explicitly frames it this way: "The conservative default: legal status questions (US work authorization, visa sponsorship) get the negative that claims nothing". Wait — re-reading: "get the negative that claims nothing, never a positive without evidence". The "why" string in the unknown branch says: "The negative claims nothing; the positive would be a fabrication."

